# Saving what the pipeline produced.
#
# TWO WAYS, for two different moments:
#
#   Right-click any viewer -> "Save image..." picks a file and writes what that
#   panel is showing, once. For "I like this, keep it."
#
#   save() in a script declares an export. Nothing is written while you tune --
#   a save that fired on every slider tick would fill a directory. File -> Run
#   script saves writes them when you say so.
#
# FORMAT comes from the extension, or from format= if you would rather say it.
# PNG and BMP are lossless 8-bit; JPEG takes quality=1..100; .hdr keeps the
# LINEAR values and is the one to use for a merged bracket, whose range cannot
# survive 8 bits.
#
# An 8-bit save goes through the same display curve the viewer draws with, so
# the file matches the screen rather than coming out dark.
#
# EXISTING FILES: "increment" by default (out.png, then out_1.png), since
# re-running a script is the normal thing to do here and silently overwriting
# the last result would be a bad surprise. "overwrite" and "skip" are the other
# two.
#
# A GROUP writes one numbered file per frame: out_001.png, out_002.png, ...

src = image("test")

src => brightness(brightness = 0.1)
    => save("export/adjusted.png")
    => display("adjusted")

# The same image as a JPEG, overwriting rather than accumulating copies.
src => save("export/preview.jpg", quality = 85, existing = "overwrite")
